      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "What is meant is that for some specific type of events we would like to control how many people can join said event, while still having enough space for staff to join, should they for example crash and want to rejoin the instance.\n\nIn general, what a \"host account\" would be used for.\n\nSome more details, let's say there are the roles \"Management\" and \"Guests\", guests are allowed to request to join the group instance and management is getting the request and they are allowed to accept it.\n\nWith that it would be possible to still have some leeway for when the instance is \"full\".",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-10-15T14:03:49.851Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Most places running events want to run the +18 instance types but can’t control the flow of people for example like a host account, and I’ve seen I happen where there’s now a queue and staff can’t get in to work the event",
